+// Power-key wake robustness on the OnePlus 6T (sdm845-mainline 6.16.7).
+// Waking the DSI panel takes ~1s, so a user pressing power on a blanked screen
+// tends to press again before it's visibly on. The first press wakes it
+// (cancels the blank, clearing _isInAction); a later press then sees no action
+// ongoing and arms a blank-on-release, which turns the screen right back off —
+// the "press it 3 times to wake" ping-pong. Guard it two ways:
+//  - drop rapid duplicate PRESS events (also covers doubled hardware events),
+//  - refuse to blank-on-release for a grace period after a power-key WAKE, so
+//    the reflexive re-presses can't turn the just-woken screen back off.
+// Releases are otherwise untouched, so pressing power to blank an in-use screen
+// still works (its wake was longer ago than the grace window).
+const POWER_PRESS_DEBOUNCE_MS = 400;
+const POWER_WAKE_GRACE_MS = 1500;
+
 Gio._promisify(Shell, 'util_start_systemd_unit');
 Gio._promisify(Shell, 'util_stop_systemd_unit');
 
